    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/museos/centrocultural.jpg"
             data-ms-field="lugares.centro-cultural-leyes-de-reforma.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Leyes de Reforma Cultural Center">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Leyes de Reforma Cultural Center
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                This historical site is directly linked to the Reform Laws era and the government of Benito Juárez during the Reform War (1858-1861). In these houses of the port of Veracruz, the liberal government was temporarily established, and from here fundamental laws for the separation of Church and State were promulgated, such as the Juárez Law, the Lerdo Law, and the nationalization of ecclesiastical property. The property was recently restored and converted into a cultural center dedicated to preserving the historical memory of Mexican liberalism and Juárez&#039;s stay in Veracruz. It was officially inaugurated as a cultural center in 2024.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
                                                                                <div class="card-item-wrapper h-full animate-fade-in" data-categorias="[&quot;museos&quot;]">
                        <a href="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/CentroHistorico/lugares/cevart-hugo-arguelles" class="group bg-[#F4F0E9] rounded-[1.5rem] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/museos/centrohugo.jpg"
             data-ms-field="lugares.cevart-hugo-arguelles.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Hugo Argüelles Veracruz Center for the Arts">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Hugo Argüelles Veracruz Center for the Arts
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                Discover CEVART, which occupies a building whose history dates back to the 18th century. Originally it was part of the walled city of Veracruz and belonged to important merchants of the port. Throughout the 19th century it had different commercial uses, including shops, a hotel, offices, and shipping agencies. In 2004 it was inaugurated as the Veracruz Center for the Arts and named after the Veracruz dramatist Hugo Argüelles. It currently functions as an important space for artistic training, workshops, exhibitions, dance, theater, and cultural activities. In 2015 it was rehabilitated and modernized to preserve the historical building and adapt it to new cultural activities.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
                                                                                <div class="card-item-wrapper h-full animate-fade-in" data-categorias="[&quot;museos&quot;]">
                        <a href="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/CentroHistorico/lugares/casa-benito-juarez" class="group bg-[#F4F0E9] rounded-[1.5rem] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/museos/casabenito.png"
             data-ms-field="lugares.casa-benito-juarez.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Benito Juárez House">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Benito Juárez House
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                This house is one of the most important historical sites related to Benito Juárez in Veracruz. During the Reform War, Juárez and part of his cabinet occupied nearby properties in the port while defending the liberal government against the conservative movement. The house was restored to function as a historical and cultural site, displaying documents, objects, and aspects of the political life of that era. It is part of the historical complex related to the Reform Laws and helps to understand the strategic role that Veracruz played as the provisional capital of Mexico during the 19th-century conflict.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
                                                                                <div class="card-item-wrapper h-full animate-fade-in" data-categorias="[&quot;museos&quot;]">
                        <a href="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/CentroHistorico/lugares/casa-principal" class="group bg-[#F4F0E9] rounded-[1.5rem] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/museos/casaprincipal.jpg"
             data-ms-field="lugares.casa-principal.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Casa Principal Cultural Center">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Casa Principal Cultural Center
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                Casa Principal is one of the oldest colonial buildings in the historic center of Veracruz. During the viceregal era it functioned as a residence and office for Spanish merchants linked to the port, taking advantage of the intense mercantile activity of the city. Over time the property had different administrative and commercial uses until it became a cultural space managed by the Veracruz Institute of Culture. Today it is mainly dedicated to contemporary art exhibitions, photography, painting, and cultural activities, preserving much of its historical architecture.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
