                        <a href="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/CentroHistorico/lugares/letras-veracruz" class="group bg-[#F4F0E9] rounded-[1.5rem] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/lugares/letrasvera.jpg"
             data-ms-field="lugares.letras-veracruz.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Veracruz Letters">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Veracruz Letters
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                The Veracruz Letters, located on the waterfront of the port of Veracruz, have become one of the most representative tourist and photographic spots in the city. This urban monument was installed as part of the efforts to strengthen the visual and cultural identity of the port, highlighting the pride of being veracruzano and the historical importance of the city as Mexico&#039;s maritime gateway. Its location facing the sea allows visitors to appreciate both port activity and the coastal landscape, making it a modern symbol that blends tradition, tourism, and daily life.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
                                                                                <div class="card-item-wrapper ficha-extra hidden h-full" data-categorias="[&quot;plazas&quot;]">
                        <a href="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/CentroHistorico/lugares/plaza-heroismo-veracruzano" class="group bg-[#F4F0E9] rounded-[1.5rem] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/lugares/plazaheroismo.jpg"
             data-ms-field="lugares.plaza-heroismo-veracruzano.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Heroismo Veracruzano Plaza">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Heroismo Veracruzano Plaza
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                The Heroismo Veracruzano Plaza is a commemorative space dedicated to remembering the different heroic deeds that marked the history of Veracruz and the country. The port was the scene of important military events, such as the defense against foreign invasions in the 19th and 20th centuries, which is why Veracruz received the title of &quot;Four Times Heroic.&quot; The plaza seeks to pay tribute to the soldiers, sailors, and citizens who participated in these historical defenses, as well as serving as a public space for coexistence and historical memory facing the waterfront.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
                                                                                <div class="card-item-wrapper ficha-extra hidden h-full" data-categorias="[&quot;edificios-emblematicos&quot;]">
                        <a href="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/CentroHistorico/lugares/teatro-de-la-reforma" class="group bg-[#F4F0E9] rounded-[1.5rem] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/lugares/teatroreforma.jpg"
             data-ms-field="lugares.teatro-de-la-reforma.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Reforma Theater">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Reforma Theater
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                The Reforma Theater is one of the most important and historical cultural buildings in Veracruz. Inaugurated in the 19th century, this venue was built during a stage of urban modernization of the port and quickly became a center for artistic, cultural, and political activities. Inside, theatrical plays, concerts, and official events of great relevance to Veracruz social life were held. Its name refers to the historical period of the Liberal Reform in Mexico, and over the years the building has been restored to preserve its architectural and cultural value as part of the historical heritage of Veracruz.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
                                                                                <div class="card-item-wrapper ficha-extra hidden h-full" data-categorias="[&quot;edificios-emblematicos&quot;]">
                        <a href="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/CentroHistorico/lugares/teatro-clavijero" class="group bg-[#F4F0E9] rounded-[1.5rem] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/lugares/teatroclavijero.jpeg"
             data-ms-field="lugares.teatro-clavijero.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Francisco J. Clavijero Theater">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Francisco J. Clavijero Theater
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                The Francisco J. Clavijero Theater is one of the most important and historical cultural venues in Veracruz, with theatrical antecedents dating back to the colonial era when the old Comedy House existed. The current building, inaugurated in 1902 during the Porfiriato, stands out for its neoclassical architecture of French influence and has been the stage for opera, theater, concerts, cinema, and historical events of the port. Throughout its history it suffered fires, name changes, and periods of restoration, until it became a cultural symbol of the historic center and took the name of the Veracruz historian Francisco Javier Clavijero.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
