    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/lugares/iglesiabuen.jpg"
             data-ms-field="lugares.parroquia-buen-viaje.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Santo Cristo del Buen Viaje Parish">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Santo Cristo del Buen Viaje Parish
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                The Santo Cristo del Buen Viaje Parish is one of the most traditional religious temples in the historic center of Veracruz. Its origin is related to the deep connection of the port with maritime activity, since for centuries sailors, travelers, and merchants went to the temple to entrust themselves before departing or to thank for their safe return. Devotion to the Santo Cristo del Buen Viaje became one of the most important religious expressions among the port community. Over time, the parish acquired historical and architectural relevance, forming part of the cultural and spiritual heritage of Veracruz.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
