    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/lugares/edificiotrigueros.jpg"
             data-ms-field="lugares.edificio-trigueros.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Trigueros Building">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Trigueros Building
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                The Trigueros Building, located facing the Veracruz Zócalo at the intersection of Mario Molina and Zaragoza streets, is an iconic structure of great historical and architectural value in the heart of the Historic Center. Built in the 19th century by merchant and philanthropist Domingo Trigueros, it stands out for its colonial arcades and Neoclassical details, having served various administrative and civic functions over the centuries.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
