    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/lugares/palacio.jpg"
             data-ms-field="lugares.palacio-municipal.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Municipal Palace (City Hall)">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Municipal Palace (City Hall)
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                The Municipal Palace of Veracruz, historically known as Casa de Cabildos, stands proudly facing the main Zócalo. It serves as the seat of the oldest municipal government in continental America, founded by Hernán Cortés in 1519. Featuring classic 17th and 18th-century neoclassical architecture, elegant arcades, and a grand central courtyard, it has been the civic epicenter of Veracruz for over five centuries.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
