    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/callejones/CallejonDesamp.jpeg"
             data-ms-field="lugares.callejon-jj-herrera.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Callejón J.J. Herrera (Callejón de los Desamparados / Callejón de la Inquisición)">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Callejón J.J. Herrera (Callejón de los Desamparados / Callejón de la Inquisición)
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                Historically known as Callejón de los Desamparados and Callejón de la Inquisición, today it bears the official name of José Joaquín Herrera. This passage was used to transfer and lock up people accused of heresy, blasphemy, or sodomy before being taken to Mexico City to be tried by the Holy Inquisition. It is closely related to the current Casa Principal, where it is believed the Tribunal of the Holy Office was located. It also stands out for its ancient constructions made with hard coral and mortar.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
