    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/callejones/PlazuelaDeLaLagunilla.png"
             data-ms-field="lugares.callejon-lagunilla.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Callejón and Plazuela de la Lagunilla">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Callejón and Plazuela de la Lagunilla
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                It is the only street in Veracruz that has preserved its name for more than 400 years. In the 17th century, the Tenoya stream passed through this site, forming a small lagoon that prevented the construction of homes. After the course was modified during the construction of the wall, the place remained as a small plaza. It stands out for its architecture similar to the alleys of Havana, the statue of Benny Moré, and for having been the setting for the film Tierra Brava in 1938.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
                                                                                <div class="card-item-wrapper ficha-extra hidden h-full" data-categorias="[&quot;callejones&quot;]">
                        <a href="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/CentroHistorico/lugares/plazuela-campana" class="group bg-[#F4F0E9] rounded-[1.5rem] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/callejones/PlazuelaDeLaCampana.png"
             data-ms-field="lugares.plazuela-campana.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Plazuela de la Campana">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Plazuela de la Campana
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                Its name comes from a bell placed by the Dominican friars to call to religious acts, since the Santo Domingo convent did not have a bell tower. In the 19th century it was also known as &quot;La Mesura&quot; due to the businesses dedicated to the weighing of merchandise. Currently, it is a traditional space for jarocho music and dance, where part of the old convent is still preserved and scenes from La Mujer del Puerto were filmed in 1934.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
                                                                                <div class="card-item-wrapper ficha-extra hidden h-full" data-categorias="[&quot;callejones&quot;]">
                        <a href="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/CentroHistorico/lugares/portal-miranda" class="group bg-[#F4F0E9] rounded-[1.5rem] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/callejones/miranda.png"
             data-ms-field="lugares.portal-miranda.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Portal de Miranda">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Portal de Miranda
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                The Callejón or Portal de Miranda, in the historic center of Veracruz, is an emblematic colonial space built in the 18th century by the Miranda family. It stood out as an important commercial center during the viceroyalty and was built with múcara stone and brick. It currently preserves its original architecture and houses the Veracruz Photo Library, dedicated to preserving historical images of the port.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
                                                                                <div class="card-item-wrapper ficha-extra hidden h-full" data-categorias="[&quot;callejones&quot;]">
                        <a href="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/CentroHistorico/lugares/callejon-clavijero" class="group bg-[#F4F0E9] rounded-[1.5rem] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/callejones/calvijero.png"
             data-ms-field="lugares.callejon-clavijero.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Callejón Clavijero">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Callejón Clavijero
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                The Callejón Clavijero, in the historic center of Veracruz, is an ancient passage named in honor of the historian and Jesuit Francisco Javier Clavijero. The area preserves traditional 19th-century architecture, old courtyards, and historical buildings linked to the colonial era, in addition to being close to important cultural spaces such as the Clavijero Theater.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
                                                                                <div class="card-item-wrapper ficha-extra hidden h-full" data-categorias="[&quot;callejones&quot;]">
                        <a href="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/CentroHistorico/lugares/callejon-tona-la-negra" class="group bg-[#F4F0E9] rounded-[1.5rem] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 flex flex-col h-full">
    <div class="relative aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-t-[1.5rem]">
        
        <img src="https://descubre.veracruzmunicipio.gob.mx/images/Centro_Historico/callejones/TonaLaNegra.png"
             data-ms-field="lugares.callejon-tona-la-negra.image"             class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
            alt="Callejón Toña la Negra">
    </div>
    
    <div class="p-5 flex flex-col flex-grow justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-1 para que el título no salte a más de una línea si es largo -->
            <h3 class="text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-sm md:text-base tracking-wider uppercase fuente-titulos line-clamp-1">
                
                Callejón Toña la Negra
            </h3>
            
            <!-- Modificado: line-clamp-3 limita el texto a 3 líneas y pone los "..." -->
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs md:text-sm font-medium font-sans mt-1.5 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">
                
                The La Huaca Neighborhood, considered the oldest sector in Veracruz, arose in the 17th century outside the old colonial wall as a refuge for African slaves and cemetery workers, taking its name from the Quechua term guaca, related to burial sites. Over time it established itself as an important Afro-mestizo neighborhood, where the first houses were made with wood from shipwrecked boats and later transformed into an area of traditional neighborhoods after the fall of the walls in 1880. In addition to preserving historical courtyards recognized by the INAH and a strong jarocha identity, La Huaca is famous for being the birthplace of musical figures like Agustín Lara and Toña la Negra, as well as for keeping alive gastronomic and cultural traditions such as the Festival of the Gorda and the Picada.
            </p>
        </div>
        
        <span class="text-[#B19657] group-hover:text-[#5C113C] font-bold text-[10px] md:text-xs tracking-wider uppercase flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors mt-2">
           LEARN MORE<span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1 duration-300">→</span>
        </span>
    </div>
</a>                    </div>
                            
        </div>

        <!-- Centered Button below the cards -->
        <div class="flex justify-center mt-12">
        
